1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,915
What's today's video about? It's about how to work a part-time job!

2
00:00:09,915 --> 00:00:11,415
Scene 1: First Greetings and Self-Introduction

3
00:00:11,415 --> 00:00:13,581
Welcome!

4
00:00:13,604 --> 00:00:16,046
Good morning!

5
00:00:16,069 --> 00:00:18,736
Good morning!

6
00:00:18,759 --> 00:00:21,770
You're starting your part-time job today, right?

7
00:00:21,794 --> 00:00:25,127
Yes, I start working today.

8
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:27,684
Nice to meet you!

9
00:00:27,707 --> 00:00:30,119
Nice to meet you!

10
00:00:30,143 --> 00:00:32,919
What's your name?

11
00:00:32,943 --> 00:00:36,343
I'm Ali.

12
00:00:36,366 --> 00:00:39,185
I'm from Malaysia.

13
00:00:39,208 --> 00:00:41,608
Ali, right?

14
00:00:41,631 --> 00:00:44,507
I'm Tanaka.

15
00:00:44,531 --> 00:00:48,418
I'm the manager of this store.

16
00:00:48,442 --> 00:00:52,290
Manager Tanaka, it's a pleasure to meet you!

17
00:00:52,313 --> 00:00:55,648
When did you come to Japan?

18
00:00:55,672 --> 00:00:58,205
I arrived last month.

19
00:00:58,228 --> 00:01:02,428
I'm currently a student at a Japanese language school.

20
00:01:02,451 --> 00:01:04,618
I see.

21
00:01:04,641 --> 00:01:07,841
Your Japanese is really good!

22
00:01:07,864 --> 00:01:11,906
Oh no, I still have a lot to learn.

23
00:01:11,930 --> 00:01:15,931
I study a lot every day.

24
00:01:15,955 --> 00:01:19,322
Is this your first part-time job?

25
00:01:19,345 --> 00:01:20,994
Yes.

26
00:01:21,017 --> 00:01:24,951
It's my first part-time job in Japan.

27
00:01:24,974 --> 00:01:28,017
I'm really nervous.

28
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:30,517
It's okay!

29
00:01:30,541 --> 00:01:33,815
Everyone feels nervous at first.

30
00:01:33,838 --> 00:01:35,572
Yes.

31
00:01:35,595 --> 00:01:38,331
But I'll do my best!

32
00:01:38,355 --> 00:01:42,133
Why do you want to work at this store?

33
00:01:42,156 --> 00:01:47,522
I want to start my own company in Japan in the future.

34
00:01:47,545 --> 00:01:53,161
So, I want to learn about Japanese business at this store.

35
00:01:53,185 --> 00:01:56,659
That's a wonderful dream!

36
00:01:56,683 --> 00:02:01,449
There are many different tasks here.

37
00:02:01,472 --> 00:02:03,039
Yes.

38
00:02:03,062 --> 00:02:06,932
I want to learn a lot of jobs!

39
00:02:06,956 --> 00:02:11,040
We have customer service, cashier work, stocking shelves, and more.

40
00:02:11,063 --> 00:02:15,863
It seems challenging, but also fun!

41
00:02:15,886 --> 00:02:17,486
Yes, it is.

42
00:02:17,509 --> 00:02:21,985
Let's start with a cheerful greeting!

43
00:02:22,008 --> 00:02:23,707
Yes.

44
00:02:23,731 --> 00:02:26,508
I'll greet everyone with energy!

45
00:02:26,532 --> 00:02:31,798
Now, let me prepare your uniform.

46
00:02:31,821 --> 00:02:33,497
Thank you!

47
00:02:33,521 --> 00:02:36,454
What size do you wear?

48
00:02:36,477 --> 00:02:38,746
Medium?

49
00:02:38,769 --> 00:02:40,785
Or large?

50
00:02:40,809 --> 00:02:43,778
Large, please.

51
00:02:43,801 --> 00:02:45,801
Got it.

52
00:02:45,824 --> 00:02:48,105
This way, please.

53
00:02:48,129 --> 00:02:49,562
Yes.

54
00:02:49,585 --> 00:02:51,718
Excuse me.

55
00:02:51,741 --> 00:03:00,750
You can download today's video script from the description and top comment.

56
00:03:00,750 --> 00:03:02,250
Scene 2: How to Use the Staff Break Room

57
00:03:02,250 --> 00:03:06,650
Ali, this is the staff break room.

58
00:03:06,673 --> 00:03:09,907
Okay. So this is the break room, right?

59
00:03:09,930 --> 00:03:14,580
Yes. Please leave your belongings on that shelf over there.

60
00:03:14,603 --> 00:03:16,536
Got it.

61
00:03:16,559 --> 00:03:19,526
The blue shelf?

62
00:03:19,549 --> 00:03:23,168
No, not the blue one.

63
00:03:23,191 --> 00:03:25,625
The white shelf next to it.

64
00:03:25,648 --> 00:03:29,528
Ah, the white shelf.

65
00:03:29,551 --> 00:03:31,805
Got it.

66
00:03:31,829 --> 00:03:36,429
There are locks, so keep your valuables in your bag.

67
00:03:36,452 --> 00:03:40,509
Got it. I’ve put them in my bag.

68
00:03:40,532 --> 00:03:43,384
Whose key is this?

69
00:03:43,407 --> 00:03:46,289
That’s my key.

70
00:03:46,313 --> 00:03:49,088
Please don’t touch it.

71
00:03:49,111 --> 00:03:52,278
Sorry. I understand.

72
00:03:52,301 --> 00:03:55,039
This is your key, Ali.

73
00:03:55,063 --> 00:03:56,902
Please use this one.

74
00:03:56,926 --> 00:03:58,659
Thank you!

75
00:03:58,682 --> 00:04:01,493
This is my key, right?

76
00:04:01,517 --> 00:04:05,083
Yes. Don’t lose it.

77
00:04:05,106 --> 00:04:07,673
I’ll be careful.

78
00:04:07,696 --> 00:04:11,296
Next, this is your uniform, Ali.

79
00:04:11,319 --> 00:04:15,092
Wow, what a nice uniform!

80
00:04:15,116 --> 00:04:17,282
There’s a cap too.

81
00:04:17,305 --> 00:04:19,182
Please wear this as well.

82
00:04:19,205 --> 00:04:22,572
Okay, I’ll wear the cap too.

83
00:04:22,595 --> 00:04:25,873
Where do I change?

84
00:04:25,897 --> 00:04:28,464
You can change in that room over there.

85
00:04:28,487 --> 00:04:31,053
That’s the changing room.

86
00:04:31,076 --> 00:04:32,743
Got it.

87
00:04:32,766 --> 00:04:35,432
The room with that door?

88
00:04:35,455 --> 00:04:38,022
Yes, that’s right.

89
00:04:38,045 --> 00:04:40,055
There’s also a name tag.

90
00:04:40,079 --> 00:04:42,612
This is your name tag, Ali.

91
00:04:42,635 --> 00:04:44,438
Thank you!

92
00:04:44,462 --> 00:04:47,337
Where should I put the name tag?

93
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:51,493
Please attach it to the left side of your uniform.

94
00:04:51,516 --> 00:04:53,794
On the left side of my uniform.

95
00:04:53,818 --> 00:04:58,351
Hey, Manager, whose shoes are these?

96
00:04:58,374 --> 00:05:01,374
Those belong to a senior staff member.

97
00:05:01,397 --> 00:05:04,364
Your shoes are over there, Ali.

98
00:05:04,387 --> 00:05:07,387
Ah, here they are!

99
00:05:07,410 --> 00:05:09,376
Great.

100
00:05:09,399 --> 00:05:11,411
Are you ready?

101
00:05:11,435 --> 00:05:14,435
Yes, I’ll go change now.

102
00:05:14,458 --> 00:05:21,563
The link to review today’s video is in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

103
00:05:21,563 --> 00:05:23,063
Scene 3: Introduction to the Part-Time Job

104
00:05:23,063 --> 00:05:28,063
Ali, the uniform looks great on you!

105
00:05:28,086 --> 00:05:29,935
Thank you!

106
00:05:29,958 --> 00:05:32,891
It’s a little embarrassing.

107
00:05:32,914 --> 00:05:37,847
Now, let me explain the store rules and schedule.

108
00:05:37,870 --> 00:05:40,004
Yes, please.

109
00:05:40,027 --> 00:05:47,793
Your part-time shifts are every Monday, Wednesday, and Friday.

110
00:05:47,816 --> 00:05:51,950
Monday, Wednesday, and Friday, right?

111
00:05:51,973 --> 00:05:53,810
Got it.

112
00:05:53,833 --> 00:05:59,474
The hours are from 4 PM to 9 PM.

113
00:05:59,497 --> 00:06:01,977
From 4 PM to 9 PM, got it.

114
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:06,842
Alright. Please come to the store at five to four.

115
00:06:06,866 --> 00:06:09,558
Five to four, got it.

116
00:06:09,581 --> 00:06:12,148
I won’t be late.

117
00:06:12,171 --> 00:06:14,626
That’s great!

118
00:06:14,649 --> 00:06:17,662
Do we get break time?

119
00:06:17,685 --> 00:06:22,918
How many hours do I need to work before getting a break?

120
00:06:22,941 --> 00:06:29,024
In this store, you get a 30-minute break after working five hours.

121
00:06:29,048 --> 00:06:32,688
A 30-minute break, okay.

122
00:06:32,711 --> 00:06:35,391
What time is the break?

123
00:06:35,415 --> 00:06:38,451
It varies depending on the day.

124
00:06:38,475 --> 00:06:42,445
Usually around 6 or 7 PM.

125
00:06:42,468 --> 00:06:44,235
Got it.

126
00:06:44,258 --> 00:06:47,991
Do we get paid during break time?

127
00:06:48,014 --> 00:06:52,492
No, you don’t get paid during breaks.

128
00:06:52,515 --> 00:06:54,764
Got it.

129
00:06:54,788 --> 00:06:57,322
What’s the hourly wage?

130
00:06:57,345 --> 00:07:01,078
The hourly wage is 1,200 yen.

131
00:07:01,101 --> 00:07:03,793
1,200 yen?

132
00:07:03,817 --> 00:07:05,983
That’s great!

133
00:07:06,006 --> 00:07:08,075
I’m happy to hear that.

134
00:07:08,099 --> 00:07:12,434
Payday is on the 25th of every month.

135
00:07:12,458 --> 00:07:16,191
We’ll deposit it directly into your bank account.

136
00:07:16,214 --> 00:07:18,481
The 25th, right.

137
00:07:18,504 --> 00:07:21,984
My account is with Mizuho Bank.

138
00:07:22,007 --> 00:07:23,879
Got it.

139
00:07:23,902 --> 00:07:26,985
You’ll need to fill out some paperwork later.

140
00:07:27,009 --> 00:07:28,642
Yes.

141
00:07:28,665 --> 00:07:30,754
I’ll do it today.

142
00:07:30,777 --> 00:07:33,777
Do you have any questions?

143
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:36,371
Is there overtime?

144
00:07:36,395 --> 00:07:40,362
Generally, there’s no overtime.

145
00:07:40,385 --> 00:07:43,868
You can leave when your shift ends.

146
00:07:43,891 --> 00:07:45,658
That’s a relief.

147
00:07:45,681 --> 00:07:48,418
Thank you!

148
00:07:48,441 --> 00:07:49,941
Scene 4: Backroom Tour / Introduction to the Store’s Backroom

149
00:07:49,941 --> 00:07:54,032
First, let me show you around the backroom today.

150
00:07:54,056 --> 00:07:56,499
The backroom, okay.

151
00:07:56,522 --> 00:07:59,522
This is pretty spacious.

152
00:07:59,545 --> 00:08:01,112
Yes, it is.

153
00:08:01,135 --> 00:08:05,135
There are a lot of products here.

154
00:08:05,158 --> 00:08:09,424
Wow, there are so many drinks over there.

155
00:08:09,448 --> 00:08:11,681
That’s right.

156
00:08:11,704 --> 00:08:16,319
That’s the cold drinks storage over there.

157
00:08:16,342 --> 00:08:20,309
Where are the hot drinks kept?

158
00:08:20,332 --> 00:08:27,765
Hot drinks are in those small boxes over there.

159
00:08:27,788 --> 00:08:30,859
Oh, in those boxes.

160
00:08:30,882 --> 00:08:33,016
Got it.

161
00:08:33,039 --> 00:08:37,519
Next, let me explain where the trash bins are.

162
00:08:37,543 --> 00:08:40,815
Where are the trash bins?

163
00:08:40,839 --> 00:08:46,258
Well, there’s a black trash bin over there.

164
00:08:46,282 --> 00:08:48,348
That’s right.

165
00:08:48,371 --> 00:08:52,654
But that’s for burnable trash.

166
00:08:52,678 --> 00:08:57,090
Where’s the PET bottle bin?

167
00:08:57,113 --> 00:09:03,113
The PET bottle bin is right next to it.

168
00:09:03,136 --> 00:09:06,936
Ah, this white one, right?

169
00:09:06,959 --> 00:09:08,559
Yes.

170
00:09:08,582 --> 00:09:13,760
In Japan, sorting trash is very important.

171
00:09:13,784 --> 00:09:15,350
Yes.

172
00:09:15,373 --> 00:09:19,783
It’s stricter than in Malaysia, so I’ll be careful.

173
00:09:19,807 --> 00:09:25,007
Also, there are scissors and pens over there.

174
00:09:25,030 --> 00:09:27,463
Do you have any tape as well?

175
00:09:27,486 --> 00:09:32,133
Yes, the tape is also up on that shelf.

176
00:09:32,157 --> 00:09:34,031
Got it.

177
00:09:34,054 --> 00:09:37,188
These are tools we use for work, right?

178
00:09:37,211 --> 00:09:39,477
That’s right.

179
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:44,307
Please make sure to return everything to its original place after use.

180
00:09:44,330 --> 00:09:48,297
I’ll put it back where it belongs.

181
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:52,955
Now, take a look at that machine over there.

182
00:09:52,979 --> 00:09:56,745
What’s that big machine?

183
00:09:56,768 --> 00:10:01,102
That’s the monitor for our security cameras.

184
00:10:01,125 --> 00:10:05,392
There are a lot of cameras inside the store.

185
00:10:05,415 --> 00:10:08,874
Wow, there sure are a lot!

186
00:10:08,898 --> 00:10:12,098
They’re important for keeping everyone safe.

187
00:10:12,121 --> 00:10:16,172
Yes, exactly.

188
00:10:16,195 --> 00:10:20,595
Now, let’s head inside the store.

189
00:10:20,619 --> 00:10:23,819
Okay, let’s go!

190
00:10:23,842 --> 00:10:25,342
Scene 5: The Basics of Customer Service – Greetings and Smiles

191
00:10:25,342 --> 00:10:29,709
Ali, this is the sales floor of the store.

192
00:10:29,732 --> 00:10:30,732
Yes.

193
00:10:30,755 --> 00:10:34,488
There are so many customers here!

194
00:10:34,511 --> 00:10:39,783
What do you think is the most important thing in customer service?

195
00:10:39,806 --> 00:10:43,940
Hmm, I’d say a smile?

196
00:10:43,963 --> 00:10:46,563
That’s right!

197
00:10:46,586 --> 00:10:51,552
A warm smile and a loud, clear greeting are essential.

198
00:10:51,575 --> 00:10:52,909
Yes.

199
00:10:52,932 --> 00:10:56,065
I’d like to practice greeting customers.

200
00:10:56,088 --> 00:10:59,580
Alright, repeat after me.

201
00:10:59,603 --> 00:11:01,578
Welcome!

202
00:11:01,602 --> 00:11:03,970
Welcome!

203
00:11:03,993 --> 00:11:05,760
Sounds good!

204
00:11:05,783 --> 00:11:10,584
But could you try speaking a little louder?

205
00:11:10,608 --> 00:11:12,851
Welcome!

206
00:11:12,874 --> 00:11:15,010
Perfect!

207
00:11:15,034 --> 00:11:19,367
Next, let’s practice the greeting for when customers check out.

208
00:11:19,390 --> 00:11:21,123
Thank you very much!

209
00:11:21,146 --> 00:11:22,780
Thank you very much!

210
00:11:22,803 --> 00:11:26,877
Your voice is so clear and lovely—it’s wonderful!

211
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:28,900
Thank you!

212
00:11:28,923 --> 00:11:31,021
I’m happy to hear that.

213
00:11:31,045 --> 00:11:35,650
What do you say when a customer enters the store?

214
00:11:35,673 --> 00:11:39,273
I say, 'Welcome!'

215
00:11:39,296 --> 00:11:43,535
And what do you say when a customer leaves?

216
00:11:43,558 --> 00:11:46,292
I say, 'Thank you very much!'

217
00:11:46,315 --> 00:11:48,395
Great job!

218
00:11:48,418 --> 00:11:51,352
You’ve got the greetings down perfectly!

219
00:11:51,375 --> 00:11:53,408
Great.

220
00:11:53,431 --> 00:11:56,031
I feel a little more confident now.

221
00:11:56,054 --> 00:12:02,821
If a customer is looking for something, you ask, 'Are you looking for something?'

222
00:12:02,844 --> 00:12:05,377
Are you looking for something?

223
00:12:05,400 --> 00:12:09,090
That’s a bit tricky, but I’ll remember it.

224
00:12:09,114 --> 00:12:12,364
No need to rush.

225
00:12:12,388 --> 00:12:14,721
Let’s take it one step at a time.

226
00:12:14,744 --> 00:12:16,077
Yes.

227
00:12:16,100 --> 00:12:19,786
I’ll greet customers loudly every day.

228
00:12:19,809 --> 00:12:24,876
Your bright voice really livens up the store!

229
00:12:24,900 --> 00:12:26,593
Thank you!

230
00:12:26,616 --> 00:12:28,788
I’ll do my best!

231
00:12:28,812 --> 00:12:30,312
Scene 6: How to Use the Cash Register

232
00:12:30,312 --> 00:12:34,520
Now, I’ll teach you how to work the cash register.

233
00:12:34,543 --> 00:12:38,809
Okay, I’m a little nervous, but I’d love to try!

234
00:12:38,832 --> 00:12:41,432
This is the cash register screen.

235
00:12:41,455 --> 00:12:44,463
The screen is a touch panel.

236
00:12:44,487 --> 00:12:47,738
The screen is big and easy to see!

237
00:12:47,761 --> 00:12:51,094
Each item has a barcode.

238
00:12:51,117 --> 00:12:54,951
Please scan the barcode using this machine.

239
00:12:54,974 --> 00:12:58,041
You'll hear a beep.

240
00:12:58,064 --> 00:13:04,431
Yes, once it beeps, the item name and price will appear on the screen.

241
00:13:04,454 --> 00:13:10,338
Oh, the screen shows 'rice ball – 150 yen'.

242
00:13:10,361 --> 00:13:12,331
That’s right.

243
00:13:12,354 --> 00:13:17,887
After scanning all the barcodes, press this 'Subtotal' button.

244
00:13:17,910 --> 00:13:20,510
The 'Subtotal' button, right?

245
00:13:20,533 --> 00:13:22,167
Pressed it.

246
00:13:22,190 --> 00:13:25,991
Next, tell the customer the total amount.

247
00:13:26,014 --> 00:13:29,547
Say, 'That'll be 150 yen.'

248
00:13:29,570 --> 00:13:32,104
That'll be 150 yen.

249
00:13:32,127 --> 00:13:34,860
The customer handed you a 1,000-yen bill.

250
00:13:34,883 --> 00:13:39,381
Enter '1000' on the screen.

251
00:13:39,404 --> 00:13:41,404
One, zero, zero, zero, right?

252
00:13:41,427 --> 00:13:43,164
Entered it.

253
00:13:43,188 --> 00:13:47,832
Then, press this 'Total' button.

254
00:13:47,855 --> 00:13:49,255
Pressed it.

255
00:13:49,278 --> 00:13:52,512
Oh, the cash drawer opened!

256
00:13:52,535 --> 00:13:54,901
How much is the change?

257
00:13:54,924 --> 00:13:57,561
Check the screen.

258
00:13:57,585 --> 00:14:03,119
The screen shows 'Change: 850 yen'.

259
00:14:03,142 --> 00:14:06,908
Hand the 850 yen to the customer.

260
00:14:06,931 --> 00:14:10,989
Count the bills and coins for the change.

261
00:14:11,012 --> 00:14:18,812
One 500-yen coin, three 100-yen coins, and one 50-yen coin.

262
00:14:18,835 --> 00:14:20,670
That’s right!

263
00:14:20,694 --> 00:14:25,261
Be careful not to mix up the amount received and the change.

264
00:14:25,284 --> 00:14:26,817
Yes.

265
00:14:26,840 --> 00:14:29,280
Double-check the numbers.

266
00:14:29,304 --> 00:14:30,804
Scene 7: Basics of Payment Confirmation at the Register

267
00:14:30,804 --> 00:14:34,970
How’s the cashier work going, Ali?

268
00:14:34,993 --> 00:14:38,442
I’m getting the hang of it a little.

269
00:14:38,466 --> 00:14:43,269
But I still get flustered sometimes.

270
00:14:43,293 --> 00:14:46,097
It's okay!

271
00:14:46,121 --> 00:14:51,587
Today, let’s go over payment confirmation at the register.

272
00:14:51,610 --> 00:14:54,810
Yes, please!

273
00:14:54,833 --> 00:15:01,200
When a customer comes to the register, you first scan their items, right?

274
00:15:01,223 --> 00:15:05,693
Yes, I can do that.

275
00:15:05,717 --> 00:15:11,483
After that, ask the customer how they’d like to pay.

276
00:15:11,506 --> 00:15:14,440
How they’d like to pay?

277
00:15:14,463 --> 00:15:18,200
Yes, it is.

278
00:15:18,223 --> 00:15:20,226
Ask, 'Will that be cash or card?'

279
00:15:20,249 --> 00:15:22,183
'Will that be cash or card?'

280
00:15:22,206 --> 00:15:25,819
Sounds good!

281
00:15:25,842 --> 00:15:27,851
Mobile payments are also common these days.

282
00:15:27,875 --> 00:15:29,716
What do I do for mobile payments?

283
00:15:29,739 --> 00:15:34,226
Scan the barcode on the customer’s phone using the register.

284
00:15:34,250 --> 00:15:38,017
Is it the same as cash or card?

285
00:15:38,040 --> 00:15:44,082
Press the same button as you would for a card.

286
00:15:44,106 --> 00:15:46,639
Press the 'Barcode Payment' button on the screen.

287
00:15:46,662 --> 00:15:49,629
Is it the same as cash or card?

288
00:15:49,652 --> 00:15:53,452
Press the same button as you would for a card.

289
00:15:53,475 --> 00:15:58,516
Press the 'Barcode Payment' button on the screen.

290
00:15:58,539 --> 00:16:02,473
The 'Barcode Payment' button, got it.

291
00:16:02,496 --> 00:16:04,662
Got it.

292
00:16:04,685 --> 00:16:11,019
If the customer uses a card, have them insert it here.

293
00:16:11,042 --> 00:16:15,208
Do they insert it themselves?

294
00:16:15,231 --> 00:16:17,842
Yes, that’s right.

295
00:16:17,866 --> 00:16:20,466
We don’t touch it.

296
00:16:20,489 --> 00:16:22,322
Got it.

297
00:16:22,345 --> 00:16:24,712
That’s safe.

298
00:16:24,735 --> 00:16:29,401
Once the payment is complete, hand the customer the receipt.

299
00:16:29,424 --> 00:16:32,191
Please ask the customer, 'Would you like your receipt?'

300
00:16:32,214 --> 00:16:34,032
Would you like your receipt?

301
00:16:34,056 --> 00:16:37,139
Yes, it is.

302
00:16:37,162 --> 00:16:42,296
Many customers say they don’t need one.

303
00:16:42,319 --> 00:16:44,085
Got it.

304
00:16:44,108 --> 00:16:46,917
Ask kindly.

305
00:16:46,941 --> 00:16:48,441
Scene 8: Customer Service for Bento Orders

306
00:16:48,441 --> 00:16:54,450
Ali, today we’ll cover customer service for bento orders.

307
00:16:54,473 --> 00:16:57,073
Customer service for bento orders?

308
00:16:57,096 --> 00:16:59,769
What do we say?

309
00:16:59,793 --> 00:17:03,041
Ask the customer, 'Would you like your bento warmed up?'

310
00:17:03,065 --> 00:17:04,631
That’s what we ask.

311
00:17:04,654 --> 00:17:08,096
Ask the customer, 'Would you like your bento warmed up?'

312
00:17:08,120 --> 00:17:15,087
If the customer says yes, put it in the microwave.

313
00:17:15,110 --> 00:17:18,476
How long do we microwave it for?

314
00:17:18,499 --> 00:17:22,554
The heating time is written on the bento bag.

315
00:17:22,578 --> 00:17:29,073
It’s usually around 50 seconds or 1 minute.

316
00:17:29,097 --> 00:17:30,730
Yes.

317
00:17:30,754 --> 00:17:35,687
Since it’s an industrial microwave, you just press the button once.

318
00:17:35,710 --> 00:17:37,644
That’s convenient!

319
00:17:37,667 --> 00:17:40,933
What do we do after heating it?

320
00:17:40,956 --> 00:17:46,556
Don’t put a warm bento with a cold drink in the same bag.

321
00:17:46,579 --> 00:17:49,746
Should we put them in separate bags?

322
00:17:49,769 --> 00:17:52,040
Yes, that’s right.

323
00:17:52,064 --> 00:17:55,297
It’s better to use separate bags.

324
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:57,087
Got it.

325
00:17:57,110 --> 00:17:59,002
I’ll be careful.

326
00:17:59,026 --> 00:18:02,793
Next, let’s confirm the bag.

327
00:18:02,816 --> 00:18:05,155
Would you like a bag?

328
00:18:05,178 --> 00:18:06,945
That’s what we ask.

329
00:18:06,968 --> 00:18:09,135
Would you like a bag?

330
00:18:09,158 --> 00:18:17,024
Bags are now charged—large ones cost five yen, and small ones cost three yen.

331
00:18:17,047 --> 00:18:19,581
Bags are not free, right?

332
00:18:19,604 --> 00:18:21,937
It will cost you.

333
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:23,960
That’s right.

334
00:18:23,983 --> 00:18:30,116
When the customer asks for a bag, press the bag button.

335
00:18:30,139 --> 00:18:31,940
Got it.

336
00:18:31,963 --> 00:18:36,096
Would you like chopsticks with your bento?

337
00:18:36,119 --> 00:18:37,494
Yes.

338
00:18:37,518 --> 00:18:40,157
Would you like chopsticks?

339
00:18:40,180 --> 00:18:42,025
Please ask them,

340
00:18:42,049 --> 00:18:44,616
Would you like chopsticks?

341
00:18:44,639 --> 00:18:47,494
Would you like a spoon as well?

342
00:18:47,517 --> 00:18:51,751
We provide a spoon for curry and doria.

343
00:18:51,774 --> 00:18:55,907
You decide between chopsticks or a spoon based on the item.

344
00:18:55,930 --> 00:18:57,430
Scene 9: Choosing Onigiri

345
00:18:57,430 --> 00:18:59,397
Welcome!

346
00:18:59,420 --> 00:19:01,557
Welcome!

347
00:19:01,581 --> 00:19:06,548
Oh, hello! Are you looking for something?

348
00:19:06,571 --> 00:19:08,740
Excuse me.

349
00:19:08,764 --> 00:19:11,764
I'd like to buy some onigiri.

350
00:19:11,787 --> 00:19:14,787
Which one is the tastiest?

351
00:19:14,810 --> 00:19:19,576
We have a great variety of onigiri here.

352
00:19:19,599 --> 00:19:23,633
Which onigiri is the most popular?

353
00:19:23,656 --> 00:19:28,193
The salmon onigiri is our bestseller.

354
00:19:28,217 --> 00:19:30,693
It's really delicious.

355
00:19:30,716 --> 00:19:32,806
Salmon?

356
00:19:32,830 --> 00:19:34,996
Sounds good!

357
00:19:35,019 --> 00:19:38,253
What other options do you have?

358
00:19:38,276 --> 00:19:42,565
We have ume (plum), kombu (kelp), and tuna mayo.

359
00:19:42,588 --> 00:19:45,421
Is the tuna mayo good?

360
00:19:45,444 --> 00:19:47,278
Yes.

361
00:19:47,301 --> 00:19:52,956
Tuna mayo is the second most popular, right after salmon.

362
00:19:52,980 --> 00:19:55,413
It's especially popular with younger customers.

363
00:19:55,436 --> 00:19:58,836
I love mayonnaise.

364
00:19:58,859 --> 00:20:01,526
I'll go with the tuna mayo.

365
00:20:01,548 --> 00:20:03,588
Thank you!

366
00:20:03,612 --> 00:20:06,269
This one is tuna mayo.

367
00:20:06,293 --> 00:20:09,972
Do you have any spicy rice balls?

368
00:20:09,995 --> 00:20:13,929
The mentaiko rice ball is a little spicy.

369
00:20:13,952 --> 00:20:15,952
Mentaiko?

370
00:20:15,975 --> 00:20:18,645
That sounds delicious too.

371
00:20:18,668 --> 00:20:23,082
Which would you prefer, mentaiko or tuna mayo?

372
00:20:23,106 --> 00:20:26,072
I'll go with tuna mayo today.

373
00:20:26,095 --> 00:20:28,187
Got it.

374
00:20:28,211 --> 00:20:29,944
Thank you!

375
00:20:29,967 --> 00:20:32,934
Please pay here.

376
00:20:32,957 --> 00:20:34,647
Yes.

377
00:20:34,671 --> 00:20:37,007
No bag needed.

378
00:20:37,030 --> 00:20:39,697
No bag, got it.

379
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:41,787
Thank you!

380
00:20:41,810 --> 00:20:43,777
That'll be 150 yen.

381
00:20:43,800 --> 00:20:45,047
Yes.

382
00:20:45,070 --> 00:20:47,804
That'll be 150 yen.

383
00:20:47,827 --> 00:20:50,193
I'll take the exact amount.

384
00:20:50,216 --> 00:20:52,074
Thank you very much!

385
00:20:52,097 --> 00:20:54,166
Thank you.

386
00:20:54,190 --> 00:20:55,690
Scene 10: Customer Service and Cigarette Numbering

387
00:20:55,690 --> 00:21:01,870
Ali, your customer service earlier was excellent.

388
00:21:01,893 --> 00:21:03,512
Thank you!

389
00:21:03,535 --> 00:21:07,702
You made explaining the rice balls so engaging.

390
00:21:07,725 --> 00:21:12,858
There’s a cigarette shelf next to the register, right?

391
00:21:12,881 --> 00:21:16,895
Yes, we have a wide selection of cigarettes.

392
00:21:16,919 --> 00:21:22,174
Customers can’t grab cigarettes themselves.

393
00:21:22,197 --> 00:21:25,274
We have to get them?

394
00:21:25,298 --> 00:21:30,236
Yes, every cigarette pack has a number.

395
00:21:30,259 --> 00:21:33,926
They’re numbered from 1 to 100.

396
00:21:33,948 --> 00:21:37,951
Do customers tell us the number?

397
00:21:37,975 --> 00:21:43,575
Yes, they’ll say something like, 'Can I get number 5?'

398
00:21:43,598 --> 00:21:45,931
Number 5, got it.

399
00:21:45,954 --> 00:21:49,087
Finding them seems tricky.

400
00:21:49,110 --> 00:21:55,969
The numbers are arranged in order from left to right, so it’s easy to spot.

401
00:21:55,992 --> 00:21:57,992
Got it.

402
00:21:58,015 --> 00:22:00,501
I’ll take my time to find it.

403
00:22:00,525 --> 00:22:05,564
There’s one more important thing when selling cigarettes.

404
00:22:05,587 --> 00:22:07,554
What’s that?

405
00:22:07,578 --> 00:22:10,857
Age verification.

406
00:22:10,880 --> 00:22:16,370
In Japan, you must be 20 to buy cigarettes.

407
00:22:16,394 --> 00:22:18,372
Twenty years old, right.

408
00:22:18,395 --> 00:22:21,462
That’s different from Malaysia.

409
00:22:21,485 --> 00:22:27,698
If the customer looks young, ask them to confirm their age on the screen.

410
00:22:27,721 --> 00:22:32,521
Should I say, 'Please press the confirmation button on the screen'?

411
00:22:32,544 --> 00:22:35,311
Yes, that’s right.

412
00:22:35,334 --> 00:22:39,934
Just say, 'Please touch the screen for verification.'

413
00:22:39,957 --> 00:22:43,334
Please touch the screen for verification.

414
00:22:43,358 --> 00:22:45,758
Perfect.

415
00:22:45,781 --> 00:22:49,876
It’s the law, so it’s very important.

416
00:22:49,900 --> 00:22:51,733
Yes.

417
00:22:51,756 --> 00:22:54,249
I’ll never forget.

418
00:22:54,273 --> 00:22:55,773
