538
00:30:28,681 --> 00:30:32,959
I’ll put them at the front.

539
00:30:32,983 --> 00:30:36,864
I'll make sure customers can buy things right away.

540
00:30:36,888 --> 00:30:40,127
Yes, it's easy to buy things here.

541
00:30:40,151 --> 00:30:44,884
Please put stickers on items that are close to their expiration date.

542
00:30:44,907 --> 00:30:48,307
Sure, I'll put the stickers on.

543
00:30:48,330 --> 00:30:51,502
I'll put discount stickers on them.

544
00:30:51,525 --> 00:30:55,492
Got it, the discount stickers.

545
00:30:55,515 --> 00:30:58,115
Great job!

546
00:30:58,138 --> 00:31:02,105
Expiration dates are really important.

547
00:31:02,128 --> 00:31:06,977
Yes, I'll check them every day without fail.

548
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:08,934
Thank you!

549
00:31:08,957 --> 00:31:11,957
Yes, I'll do my best.

550
00:31:11,980 --> 00:31:14,467
Nice to meet you!

551
00:31:14,490 --> 00:31:19,057
You can count on me.

552
00:31:19,080 --> 00:31:20,580
Scene 15: Store Cleaning Lesson

553
00:31:20,580 --> 00:31:26,013
Ali, please clean the store floor.

554
00:31:26,036 --> 00:31:29,003
Okay, I'll clean it.

555
00:31:29,026 --> 00:31:32,492
Use the mop over there.

556
00:31:32,515 --> 00:31:35,849
Alright, the mop.

557
00:31:35,872 --> 00:31:41,105
Be careful since there are a lot of customers around.

558
00:31:41,128 --> 00:31:44,695
Yes, I'll be careful.

559
00:31:44,718 --> 00:31:48,084
The area near the entrance is dirty.

560
00:31:48,107 --> 00:31:52,127
Okay, I'll clean the entrance.

561
00:31:52,150 --> 00:31:58,162
The store entrance is important, so please keep it clean.

562
00:31:58,186 --> 00:32:01,245
Sure, I'll make sure it's clean.

563
00:32:01,268 --> 00:32:05,525
It gets especially dirty on rainy days.

564
00:32:05,549 --> 00:32:08,549
Yes, it's raining today.

565
00:32:08,572 --> 00:32:13,106
Since it's raining today, it'll get dirty quickly.

566
00:32:13,129 --> 00:32:15,218
That’s right.

567
00:32:15,241 --> 00:32:18,041
Please clean it a few times.

568
00:32:18,064 --> 00:32:22,398
Okay, I'll clean it a few times.

569
00:32:22,420 --> 00:32:26,387
Keeping the store clean is our top priority.

570
00:32:26,410 --> 00:32:30,043
Yes, cleanliness is key.

571
00:32:30,066 --> 00:32:32,670
It's very important.

572
00:32:32,694 --> 00:32:37,227
I'll make sure customers can shop comfortably.

573
00:32:37,250 --> 00:32:42,055
Yes, I want them to have a pleasant shopping experience.

574
00:32:42,078 --> 00:32:45,845
Do you know how to use the mop?

575
00:32:45,868 --> 00:32:49,148
Yes, I do.

576
00:32:49,171 --> 00:32:52,305
Use a little detergent, please.

577
00:32:52,328 --> 00:32:56,624
Okay, I'll use some detergent.

578
00:32:56,648 --> 00:33:01,781
Be careful not to make the floor slippery.

579
00:33:01,804 --> 00:33:05,676
Sure, I'll make sure it's not slippery.

580
00:33:05,700 --> 00:33:09,667
After cleaning, please wash the mop.

581
00:33:09,690 --> 00:33:13,623
Okay, I'll wash the mop.

582
00:33:13,646 --> 00:33:15,379
Thank you.

583
00:33:15,402 --> 00:33:17,736
I'm counting on you.

584
00:33:17,759 --> 00:33:21,175
Sure, I'll make sure it's clean.

585
00:33:21,199 --> 00:33:23,638
You can leave it to me.

586
00:33:23,661 --> 00:33:25,161
Scene 16: Basics of Toilet Cleaning

587
00:33:25,161 --> 00:33:29,294
Ali, the toilet is dirty.

588
00:33:29,317 --> 00:33:32,287
Okay, I'll clean it right away.

589
00:33:32,311 --> 00:33:36,244
The toilet cleaning supplies are over there.

590
00:33:36,267 --> 00:33:39,234
Got it, over there.

591
00:33:39,256 --> 00:33:41,990
Please wear gloves.

592
00:33:42,013 --> 00:33:45,346
Okay, I'll put on gloves.

593
00:33:45,369 --> 00:33:50,336
The toilet might be the most noticed place by customers.

594
00:33:50,359 --> 00:33:53,959
Yes, it's very important.

595
00:33:53,982 --> 00:33:58,448
Use detergent and scrub it clean.

596
00:33:58,471 --> 00:34:01,871
Sure, I'll scrub it clean.

597
00:34:01,894 --> 00:34:05,628
Don't forget to wipe the floors as well.

598
00:34:05,651 --> 00:34:08,547
Yes, I'll wipe the floors too.

599
00:34:08,570 --> 00:34:11,570
Please be mindful of any odors.

600
00:34:11,593 --> 00:34:15,193
Sure, I'll put out some air freshener.

601
00:34:15,216 --> 00:34:16,906
Thank you!

602
00:34:16,930 --> 00:34:18,897
That would be a big help.

603
00:34:18,920 --> 00:34:22,187
No problem, it's just my part-time job.

604
00:34:22,210 --> 00:34:25,578
Cleaning the restroom is tough, isn't it?

605
00:34:25,601 --> 00:34:30,176
Yeah, but it feels great when it's clean.

606
00:34:30,200 --> 00:34:32,038
I agree.

607
00:34:32,061 --> 00:34:35,400
Let's do our best for the customers.

608
00:34:35,424 --> 00:34:38,591
Yes, I'll do my best.

609
00:34:38,614 --> 00:34:41,580
Let me know when you're done.

610
00:34:41,603 --> 00:34:45,137
Yes, I'll report back when I finish.

611
00:34:45,160 --> 00:34:48,410
Make sure to wash your hands well.

612
00:34:48,434 --> 00:34:51,450
Yes, I'll wash them thoroughly.

613
00:34:51,473 --> 00:34:53,506
Thank you!

614
00:34:53,529 --> 00:34:56,734
Alright, I'll finish up quickly.

615
00:34:56,758 --> 00:34:59,053
Nice to meet you!

616
00:34:59,076 --> 00:35:02,544
Yes, I'll go clean it up nicely.

617
00:35:02,568 --> 00:35:04,068
Scene 17: Checking and Restocking Inventory

618
00:35:04,068 --> 00:35:08,684
Ali, there are no products on the shelf.

619
00:35:08,708 --> 00:35:11,179
Yes, it looks like we're sold out.

620
00:35:11,202 --> 00:35:15,571
There might be some somewhere, so please check.

621
00:35:15,595 --> 00:35:18,169
Sure, I'll look for them.

622
00:35:18,193 --> 00:35:21,206
Did you check the backroom?

623
00:35:21,229 --> 00:35:23,862
No, not yet.

624
00:35:23,885 --> 00:35:26,085
I'll check now.

625
00:35:26,108 --> 00:35:28,075
Thank you!

626
00:35:28,098 --> 00:35:30,754
We sold a lot, didn't we?

627
00:35:30,778 --> 00:35:34,660
Yes, it's been really busy.

628
00:35:34,683 --> 00:35:38,216
If you find stock, please restock the shelves right away.

629
00:35:38,239 --> 00:35:41,322
Yes, I'll restock them immediately.

630
00:35:41,346 --> 00:35:45,603
If there's no stock, let me know.

631
00:35:45,627 --> 00:35:49,794
Yes, I'll let you know if there's none left.

632
00:35:49,817 --> 00:35:51,250
Thank you.

633
00:35:51,273 --> 00:35:55,326
This product is really popular.

634
00:35:55,349 --> 00:35:58,442
Yes, I like it too.

635
00:35:58,466 --> 00:36:01,633
Customers might be looking for it.

636
00:36:01,656 --> 00:36:05,733
Yes, they might come looking for it.

637
00:36:05,757 --> 00:36:08,242
Hope you find it soon.

638
00:36:08,265 --> 00:36:11,798
Yes, I'll do my best to find it.

639
00:36:11,821 --> 00:36:16,459
The backroom is well-organized, so it should be easy to spot.

640
00:36:16,482 --> 00:36:19,682
Yes, it's easy to see.

641
00:36:19,705 --> 00:36:21,581
Thank you!

642
00:36:21,604 --> 00:36:25,004
Alright, I'll be right back.

643
00:36:25,027 --> 00:36:27,194
I'm counting on you.

644
00:36:27,217 --> 00:36:29,684
Yes, I'll go now.

645
00:36:29,707 --> 00:36:32,273
I'll look for it right away.

646
00:36:32,296 --> 00:36:33,796
Scene 18: First Paycheck

647
00:36:33,796 --> 00:36:38,132
Ali, today is payday!

648
00:36:38,156 --> 00:36:41,489
Yes, it's payday!

649
00:36:41,512 --> 00:36:44,312
I'm really looking forward to it.

650
00:36:44,335 --> 00:36:47,585
Did you check your bank account?

651
00:36:47,609 --> 00:36:50,942
Yes, I checked it.

652
00:36:50,965 --> 00:36:53,532
The money is there!

653
00:36:53,555 --> 00:36:56,088
That's great, isn't it?

654
00:36:56,111 --> 00:36:59,445
It's the money you worked hard for.

655
00:36:59,468 --> 00:37:03,104
Yes, I'm so happy.

656
00:37:03,128 --> 00:37:07,378
What are you going to spend your first paycheck on?

657
00:37:07,402 --> 00:37:11,402
I'll buy a gift for my parents.

658
00:37:11,425 --> 00:37:14,558
I'll send it to my family in Malaysia.

659
00:37:14,581 --> 00:37:17,314
That's wonderful.

660
00:37:17,337 --> 00:37:20,704
Your family will be thrilled.

661
00:37:20,727 --> 00:37:24,093
Yes, I think they'll be happy.

662
00:37:24,116 --> 00:37:28,370
Aren't you going to buy something for yourself?

663
00:37:28,394 --> 00:37:30,194
I agree.

664
00:37:30,217 --> 00:37:34,183
I want some new clothes from Japan.

665
00:37:34,206 --> 00:37:36,240
Clothes?

666
00:37:36,263 --> 00:37:38,349
Nice!

667
00:37:38,373 --> 00:37:42,252
Yes, I'll go shopping this weekend.

668
00:37:42,276 --> 00:37:45,476
It's a well-deserved reward for your hard work.

669
00:37:45,499 --> 00:37:48,432
Yes, it's my reward.

670
00:37:48,455 --> 00:37:51,954
Let's keep up the good work on your next job too.

671
00:37:51,978 --> 00:37:56,111
Yes, I'll do my best on the next job too.

672
00:37:56,134 --> 00:38:00,068
Ali, you're already an asset to the store.

673
00:38:00,090 --> 00:38:02,327
Yes, thank you very much.

674
00:38:02,350 --> 00:38:05,566
I look forward to working with you from now on.

675
00:38:05,589 --> 00:38:09,806
Yes, I look forward to working with you too.

676
00:38:09,830 --> 00:38:13,796
I'm really happy about my paycheck.

677
00:38:13,819 --> 00:38:15,319
Scene 19: Handling Change Mistakes

678
00:38:15,319 --> 00:38:18,353
Ali, I'm sorry.

679
00:38:18,375 --> 00:38:22,056
I made a mistake with the change.

680
00:38:22,080 --> 00:38:25,214
Yes, what happened?

681
00:38:25,237 --> 00:38:30,403
I gave a customer 100 yen too much.

682
00:38:30,426 --> 00:38:33,305
That's a problem.

683
00:38:33,329 --> 00:38:36,804
Does the register balance?

684
00:38:36,827 --> 00:38:40,594
No, we're 100 yen short.

685
00:38:40,617 --> 00:38:43,850
I'll report it to the manager.

686
00:38:43,873 --> 00:38:47,540
I'm sorry. Thank you.

687
00:38:47,563 --> 00:38:50,622
Is the customer still here?

688
00:38:50,645 --> 00:38:54,462
No, they've already left.

689
00:38:54,486 --> 00:38:56,552
That's too bad.

690
00:38:56,575 --> 00:39:00,545
But everyone makes mistakes.

691
00:39:00,569 --> 00:39:03,585
I’ll be careful.

692
00:39:03,609 --> 00:39:06,942
I used to make mistakes all the time too.

693
00:39:06,965 --> 00:39:08,774
Really?

694
00:39:08,798 --> 00:39:11,216
That’s a relief.

695
00:39:11,239 --> 00:39:15,173
Let's take our time and double-check next time.

696
00:39:15,196 --> 00:39:18,612
Yes, I'll double-check carefully.

697
00:39:18,635 --> 00:39:22,401
Let's check the register amount again.

698
00:39:22,424 --> 00:39:25,430
Yes, let's check it together.

699
00:39:25,454 --> 00:39:29,454
It's important to correct mistakes quickly.

700
00:39:29,476 --> 00:39:32,410
Yes, I'll fix it right away.

701
00:39:32,433 --> 00:39:34,599
Don't worry about it.

702
00:39:34,622 --> 00:39:36,189
Thank you!

703
00:39:36,212 --> 00:39:39,845
Yes, let's be more careful from now on.

704
00:39:39,868 --> 00:39:41,802
Yes, thank you very much.

705
00:39:41,825 --> 00:39:44,491
Let's keep up the good work.

706
00:39:44,514 --> 00:39:46,014
Scene 20: A Lesson on Microwave Mishaps

707
00:39:46,014 --> 00:39:52,449
Ali, I tried heating my lunch in the microwave, but I messed up.

708
00:39:52,473 --> 00:39:56,040
Yes. What happened?

709
00:39:56,063 --> 00:40:01,430
I microwaved it for too long, and the container melted.

710
00:40:01,453 --> 00:40:04,546
Oh no, that’s terrible!

711
00:40:04,569 --> 00:40:08,261
Was the customer upset?

712
00:40:08,284 --> 00:40:13,919
No, they weren’t upset, but I still feel bad.

713
00:40:13,943 --> 00:40:18,201
I’ll replace it with a new bento for you.

714
00:40:18,224 --> 00:40:19,918
Thank you!

715
00:40:19,942 --> 00:40:22,013
Excuse me.

716
00:40:22,036 --> 00:40:25,803
Is the microwave time okay now?

717
00:40:25,827 --> 00:40:29,960
Yes, the time is written on the bag.

718
00:40:29,983 --> 00:40:33,150
I’ll make sure to check it carefully from now on.

719
00:40:33,173 --> 00:40:36,251
Yes, please double-check it.

720
00:40:36,275 --> 00:40:40,133
The microwave gets really hot, you know.

721
00:40:40,156 --> 00:40:43,756
Yes, it gets *very* hot.

722
00:40:43,779 --> 00:40:46,579
Be careful not to burn yourself.

723
00:40:46,602 --> 00:40:50,369
Yes, I’ll be careful while working.

724
00:40:50,392 --> 00:40:53,480
Is the bento okay now?

725
00:40:53,503 --> 00:40:57,636
Yes, we have a new one ready.

726
00:40:57,659 --> 00:40:59,718
Great.

727
00:40:59,742 --> 00:41:02,875
Let’s apologize to the customer.

728
00:41:02,898 --> 00:41:05,665
Yes, I’ll apologize.

729
00:41:05,688 --> 00:41:09,254
Was the customer a kind person?

730
00:41:09,277 --> 00:41:12,644
Yes, they were very kind.

731
00:41:12,667 --> 00:41:15,500
That’s a relief, then.

732
00:41:15,523 --> 00:41:18,591
Yes, I feel relieved.

733
00:41:18,615 --> 00:41:21,418
I won’t make the same mistake again.

734
00:41:21,441 --> 00:41:24,724
Yes, let’s do our best!

735
00:41:24,747 --> 00:41:27,680
Let’s check it together.

736
00:41:27,703 --> 00:41:30,639
Yes, thank you very much.

737
00:41:30,663 --> 00:41:32,163
Scene 21: Practicing Customer Service

738
00:41:32,163 --> 00:41:37,844
Ali, that customer is looking for a cold drink.

739
00:41:37,868 --> 00:41:42,083
Sure. What kind of drink would they like?

740
00:41:42,106 --> 00:41:46,440
Ask if they prefer tea or juice.

741
00:41:46,463 --> 00:41:49,359
Okay, I’ll ask them.

742
00:41:49,382 --> 00:41:53,230
Excuse me, would you like tea?

743
00:41:53,254 --> 00:41:56,388
Or would you prefer juice?

744
00:41:56,411 --> 00:42:00,744
The customer says they’d like green tea.

745
00:42:00,767 --> 00:42:02,740
Got it.

746
00:42:02,763 --> 00:42:06,302
The chilled green tea is over there.

747
00:42:06,325 --> 00:42:09,801
Please guide them there.

748
00:42:09,825 --> 00:42:12,758
Right this way, please.

749
00:42:12,781 --> 00:42:16,026
This green tea is very popular.

750
00:42:16,050 --> 00:42:19,301
You’re guiding them so politely!

751
00:42:19,324 --> 00:42:21,257
Thank you!

752
00:42:21,280 --> 00:42:24,914
The customer looked happy.

753
00:42:24,937 --> 00:42:27,748
That’s great to hear!

754
00:42:27,771 --> 00:42:32,738
Next, let’s show them where the sodas are.

755
00:42:32,761 --> 00:42:37,604
Sure! Sodas are really popular too.

756
00:42:37,628 --> 00:42:42,637
Yes, the cola and cider are on that shelf over there.

757
00:42:42,660 --> 00:42:45,994
Got it, over there.

758
00:42:46,017 --> 00:42:49,704
The cola is on the bottom shelf.

759
00:42:49,727 --> 00:42:52,337
You know the store so well!

760
00:42:52,361 --> 00:42:56,937
Yes, I restock the shelves every day.

761
00:42:56,960 --> 00:42:59,227
That’s wonderful!

762
00:42:59,251 --> 00:43:01,146
Thank you!

763
00:43:01,169 --> 00:43:04,936
Please keep the tea shelves neat too.

764
00:43:04,959 --> 00:43:08,193
Yes, I’ll arrange them nicely.

765
00:43:08,216 --> 00:43:11,390
You're so dedicated, Ali!

766
00:43:11,413 --> 00:43:15,429
Yes, I really like this store.

767
00:43:15,453 --> 00:43:16,953
Scene 22: Helping a Customer Find Their Lost Wallet

768
00:43:16,953 --> 00:43:20,219
How can I help you, ma'am?

769
00:43:20,242 --> 00:43:21,809
Excuse me.

770
00:43:21,832 --> 00:43:24,865
I've lost my wallet.

771
00:43:24,888 --> 00:43:27,688
Did you shop here?

772
00:43:27,711 --> 00:43:30,603
No, not yet.

773
00:43:30,627 --> 00:43:34,193
I might have dropped it before entering the store.

774
00:43:34,216 --> 00:43:36,883
Where did you walk?

775
00:43:36,907 --> 00:43:40,140
I walked along the street in front of this store.

776
00:43:40,163 --> 00:43:42,530
Let's look for it together.

777
00:43:42,553 --> 00:43:44,130
Thank you!

778
00:43:44,153 --> 00:43:47,153
How about around the potted plants?

779
00:43:47,176 --> 00:43:50,254
I checked, but it wasn't there.

780
00:43:50,278 --> 00:43:52,944
What about that corner over there?

781
00:43:52,967 --> 00:43:56,901
Oh, there's something there!

782
00:43:56,924 --> 00:43:59,169
Is that a wallet?

783
00:43:59,193 --> 00:44:02,832
Yes, that's my wallet!

784
00:44:02,855 --> 00:44:05,022
Great.

785
00:44:05,045 --> 00:44:07,611
I'm so relieved!

786
00:44:07,634 --> 00:44:10,111
Is everything still inside?

787
00:44:10,135 --> 00:44:13,581
Yes, everything's here.

788
00:44:13,605 --> 00:44:15,495
That’s a relief.

789
00:44:15,518 --> 00:44:18,284
Thank you so much!

790
00:44:18,307 --> 00:44:20,759
You're such a kind store.

791
00:44:20,783 --> 00:44:23,616
I'm just glad we found it.

792
00:44:23,639 --> 00:44:26,672
Please take care on your way home.

793
00:44:26,695 --> 00:44:29,552
Yes, thank you very much.

794
00:44:29,576 --> 00:44:32,509
Would you like to do some shopping?

795
00:44:32,532 --> 00:44:35,627
Yes, I'll buy some water.

796
00:44:35,651 --> 00:44:37,785
Here you go.

797
00:44:37,808 --> 00:44:39,308
Scene 23: Training a New Staff Member

798
00:44:39,308 --> 00:44:43,908
Ali, we have a new staff member starting today.

799
00:44:43,931 --> 00:44:45,208
Yes.

800
00:44:45,232 --> 00:44:47,168
Is it a man?

801
00:44:47,192 --> 00:44:48,858
Or a woman?

802
00:44:48,881 --> 00:44:51,815
A Japanese university student.

803
00:44:51,838 --> 00:44:55,438
Ali, could you show them the ropes?

804
00:44:55,461 --> 00:44:57,061
Yes.

805
00:44:57,084 --> 00:44:59,650
I'll teach them.

806
00:44:59,673 --> 00:45:04,317
It's their first time, so please be gentle.

807
00:45:04,341 --> 00:45:05,979
Yes.

808
00:45:06,002 --> 00:45:08,569
I'll be gentle.

809
00:45:08,592 --> 00:45:09,880
Hello!

810
00:45:09,904 --> 00:45:12,270
I'm Ali.

811
00:45:12,293 --> 00:45:14,983
This is Ken.

812
00:45:15,007 --> 00:45:20,423
Ken, please learn how to use the register from Ali.

813
00:45:20,446 --> 00:45:22,688
Hello, Ken!

814
00:45:22,711 --> 00:45:26,511
Using the register isn't difficult at all.

815
00:45:26,534 --> 00:45:29,067
Ali, I'm counting on you.

816
00:45:29,090 --> 00:45:30,929
Yes.

817
00:45:30,953 --> 00:45:33,192
First, press here.

818
00:45:33,215 --> 00:45:36,282
Do you understand, Ken?

819
00:45:36,305 --> 00:45:39,338
Ken, look here.

820
00:45:39,361 --> 00:45:42,361
Scan the barcode here.

821
00:45:42,384 --> 00:45:46,237
Ali, you explain things so well!

822
00:45:46,261 --> 00:45:47,961
Thank you!

823
00:45:47,984 --> 00:45:50,865
You'll get used to it little by little.

824
00:45:50,889 --> 00:45:54,302
Ken, do your best!

825
00:45:54,325 --> 00:45:55,665
Yes.

826
00:45:55,689 --> 00:45:58,135
Let's do our best together!

827
00:45:58,158 --> 00:46:01,825
If anything comes up, just call me.

828
00:46:01,848 --> 00:46:03,581
Yes.

829
00:46:03,604 --> 00:46:05,683
I might call you.

830
00:46:05,706 --> 00:46:09,040
Ali, you're already a senior now.

831
00:46:09,062 --> 00:46:10,829
Yes.

832
00:46:10,852 --> 00:46:13,485
I'll do my best as a senior.

833
00:46:13,508 --> 00:46:15,008
Scene 24: Customer Service on Rainy Days

834
00:46:15,008 --> 00:46:19,242
Ali, it's starting to rain.

835
00:46:19,265 --> 00:46:23,708
Yes, it's really pouring outside.

836
00:46:23,731 --> 00:46:27,098
We have special services for rainy days.

837
00:46:27,121 --> 00:46:30,921
Okay, what kind of services?

838
00:46:30,944 --> 00:46:35,477
Please prepare plastic umbrellas at the entrance.

839
00:46:35,500 --> 00:46:39,870
Sure, I'll get the plastic umbrellas ready.

840
00:46:39,894 --> 00:46:45,060
Customers will bring their umbrellas on rainy days.

841
00:46:45,083 --> 00:46:49,138
Right, we'll need umbrella bags.

842
00:46:49,162 --> 00:46:51,563
That’s right.

843
00:46:51,586 --> 00:46:54,881
Please place the umbrella bags at the entrance.

844
00:46:54,905 --> 00:46:57,483
Got it, I've placed them.

845
00:46:57,506 --> 00:47:00,563
We want to make sure our customers don't get wet.

846
00:47:00,586 --> 00:47:02,645
Thank you!

847
00:47:02,669 --> 00:47:07,235
Also, the entrance can get slippery.

848
00:47:07,258 --> 00:47:10,991
Yes, I'll clean the floor.

849
00:47:11,014 --> 00:47:14,508
Please be careful not to slip.

850
00:47:14,532 --> 00:47:17,499
I will, thank you.

851
00:47:17,522 --> 00:47:22,089
There might be fewer customers on rainy days.

852
00:47:22,112 --> 00:47:27,005
Yes, but I'll restock the bread.

853
00:47:27,028 --> 00:47:28,995
Sounds good!

854
00:47:29,018 --> 00:47:33,426
Hot drinks sell well on rainy days.

855
00:47:33,450 --> 00:47:36,934
Okay, I'll prepare plenty.

856
00:47:36,958 --> 00:47:40,958
Ali, you're very attentive.

857
00:47:40,981 --> 00:47:43,865
Thank you, I'm happy to hear that.

858
00:47:43,888 --> 00:47:46,422
Hopefully, the rain will stop soon.

859
00:47:46,445 --> 00:47:49,855
Yes, I hope it stops.

860
00:47:49,878 --> 00:47:51,645
Let's do our best.

861
00:47:51,668 --> 00:47:54,744
Yes, I'll do my best.

862
00:47:54,768 --> 00:47:56,268
Scene 25: Basics of Operating a Cash Register

863
00:47:56,268 --> 00:48:00,601
Ali, it's really busy today, isn't it?

864
00:48:00,624 --> 00:48:06,643
Yes, it's lunchtime, so there are a lot of customers.

865
00:48:06,666 --> 00:48:10,684
Many customers are buying bento boxes.

866
00:48:10,708 --> 00:48:15,241
Yes, I'm checking them out one after another.

867
00:48:15,264 --> 00:48:19,161
Don't rush, let's do it carefully.

868
00:48:19,185 --> 00:48:22,643
Okay, I'll do it carefully.

869
00:48:22,666 --> 00:48:26,099
Make sure not to make any mistakes with the change.

870
00:48:26,122 --> 00:48:29,797
Yes, I'll double-check the change.

871
00:48:29,821 --> 00:48:33,255
Do you want to heat this up?

872
00:48:33,278 --> 00:48:35,495
That’s what we ask.

873
00:48:35,518 --> 00:48:38,285
Yes, would you like it heated?

874
00:48:38,308 --> 00:48:39,980
That’s what we ask.

875
00:48:40,003 --> 00:48:43,006
Don't forget to include chopsticks.

876
00:48:43,029 --> 00:48:46,563
Okay, I'll include chopsticks.

877
00:48:46,586 --> 00:48:49,352
Keep up the good work at the register.

878
00:48:49,375 --> 00:48:52,226
Yes, I'll do my best.

879
00:48:52,250 --> 00:48:55,746
Please say, 'Thank you for waiting.'

880
00:48:55,770 --> 00:48:57,904
Thank you for waiting.

881
00:48:57,927 --> 00:49:00,660
You have a very nice voice.

882
00:49:00,683 --> 00:49:02,320
Thank you!

883
00:49:02,344 --> 00:49:06,918
The busy time will be over soon.

884
00:49:06,941 --> 00:49:10,075
Yes, I'll do my best.

885
00:49:10,098 --> 00:49:15,264
When it's busy, teamwork is the key.

886
00:49:15,287 --> 00:49:18,121
Yes, I'll work together with everyone.

887
00:49:18,144 --> 00:49:20,311
Are you tired?

888
00:49:20,334 --> 00:49:23,378
No, I'm fine.

889
00:49:23,402 --> 00:49:26,048
Let's take a break when we're done.

890
00:49:26,071 --> 00:49:29,139
Yes, let's take a break.

891
00:49:29,162 --> 00:49:30,662
Scene 26: Giving Directions – Practice Session

892
00:49:30,662 --> 00:49:34,662
The customer is asking, 'Where is the station?'

893
00:49:34,685 --> 00:49:36,923
They're asking.

894
00:49:36,946 --> 00:49:40,199
Yes, the station.

895
00:49:40,223 --> 00:49:44,189
Turn right at this corner.

896
00:49:44,212 --> 00:49:48,419
Is there a road after that?

897
00:49:48,443 --> 00:49:53,179
Then, walk straight ahead.

898
00:49:53,203 --> 00:49:55,483
Is it far?

899
00:49:55,506 --> 00:49:59,174
No, it's about five minutes away.

900
00:49:59,198 --> 00:50:02,631
They're saying, 'Thank you.'

901
00:50:02,654 --> 00:50:06,988
No, you're welcome.

902
00:50:07,011 --> 00:50:11,144
Ali, you're great at giving directions!

903
00:50:11,167 --> 00:50:15,384
Yes, because I checked the map.

904
00:50:15,408 --> 00:50:19,057
The customer looked happy.

905
00:50:19,080 --> 00:50:22,413
Yes, that's great.

906
00:50:22,436 --> 00:50:26,408
Giving directions in Japanese must be difficult.

907
00:50:26,432 --> 00:50:32,515
Yes, it's a little tough, but I'm happy to help.

908
00:50:32,538 --> 00:50:35,272
You were really helpful.

909
00:50:35,295 --> 00:50:38,828
Yes, I was glad to help.

910
00:50:38,851 --> 00:50:44,097
Are there any other tourist spots nearby?

911
00:50:44,120 --> 00:50:49,320
Yes, there's a big park over there.

912
00:50:49,343 --> 00:50:53,576
Oh, that sounds great for a walk.

913
00:50:53,599 --> 00:50:56,877
Yes, it's really nice.

914
00:50:56,900 --> 00:51:01,542
Thanks to you, Ali, the customer felt at ease.

915
00:51:01,566 --> 00:51:04,541
Yes, that's great.

916
00:51:04,564 --> 00:51:07,697
We'll count on you in the future too.

917
00:51:07,720 --> 00:51:10,854
Yes, I'll do my best.

918
00:51:10,877 --> 00:51:12,377
Scene 27: Break Time Chit-Chat

919
00:51:12,377 --> 00:51:16,636
Ali, it's break time.

920
00:51:16,659 --> 00:51:19,459
Yes, thank you.

921
00:51:19,482 --> 00:51:21,915
What are you going to eat?

922
00:51:21,938 --> 00:51:25,705
I'm having onigiri.

923
00:51:25,728 --> 00:51:29,494
I'll have a sandwich.

924
00:51:29,517 --> 00:51:33,451
What do you usually do during break?

925
00:51:33,474 --> 00:51:37,607
I often listen to music.

926
00:51:37,630 --> 00:51:40,397
Japanese music?

927
00:51:40,420 --> 00:51:45,020
Yes, I've been into J-pop lately.

928
00:51:45,043 --> 00:51:47,921
Whose music do you like?

929
00:51:47,945 --> 00:51:52,145
I love YOASOBI.

930
00:51:52,168 --> 00:51:54,343
I like them too!

931
00:51:54,366 --> 00:51:57,299
They're really popular, aren't they?

932
00:51:57,322 --> 00:52:01,189
Yes, their lyrics are so interesting.

933
00:52:01,212 --> 00:52:04,745
Do you listen to Malaysian music too?

934
00:52:04,768 --> 00:52:09,337
Yes, Malaysian songs are wonderful too.

935
00:52:09,361 --> 00:52:11,761
You'll have to introduce me to some later.

936
00:52:11,784 --> 00:52:15,384
Sure, you should definitely listen!

937
00:52:15,407 --> 00:52:20,440
Break time is short but important.

938
00:52:20,463 --> 00:52:23,796
Yes, it helps me recharge.

939
00:52:23,819 --> 00:52:27,264
Let's do our best for the afternoon shift too.

940
00:52:27,288 --> 00:52:30,098
Yes, I'll do my best.

941
00:52:30,122 --> 00:52:34,539
I'll take over the register when break is over.

942
00:52:34,562 --> 00:52:36,563
Yes, please show me.

943
00:52:36,586 --> 00:52:39,237
I feel so refreshed.

944
00:52:39,261 --> 00:52:40,761
Scene 28: Closing Time – Wrapping Up for the Day

945
00:52:40,761 --> 00:52:45,213
Ali, it's almost time to head home.

946
00:52:45,237 --> 00:52:48,525
Yes, it's 9 o'clock.

947
00:52:48,548 --> 00:52:51,044
Thank you for everything today.

948
00:52:51,067 --> 00:52:54,242
You too—great job today!

949
00:52:54,265 --> 00:52:57,532
Let's balance the cash register.

950
00:52:57,555 --> 00:53:00,788
Sure, let's count it.

951
00:53:00,811 --> 00:53:03,544
Does the cash add up?

952
00:53:03,567 --> 00:53:06,457
Yes, it's perfect.

953
00:53:06,481 --> 00:53:08,548
Great.

954
00:53:08,571 --> 00:53:11,772
The cleanup looks flawless too.

955
00:53:11,795 --> 00:53:15,363
Yep, I finished cleaning.

956
00:53:15,387 --> 00:53:18,605
Did you take out the trash?

957
00:53:18,629 --> 00:53:21,232
Yes, I did.

958
00:53:21,255 --> 00:53:22,937
Thank you!

959
00:53:22,961 --> 00:53:26,094
You're so reliable.

960
00:53:26,117 --> 00:53:29,129
Oh, it's nothing.

961
00:53:29,153 --> 00:53:31,772
Our next shift is the day after tomorrow, right?

962
00:53:31,796 --> 00:53:35,164
Yes, the day after tomorrow.

963
00:53:35,187 --> 00:53:38,020
Looking forward to seeing you then.

964
00:53:38,043 --> 00:53:41,294
I’ll be waiting!

965
00:53:41,318 --> 00:53:44,085
I'll head out first.

966
00:53:44,108 --> 00:53:46,475
Take care—great work today!

967
00:53:46,498 --> 00:53:48,866
Take care—great work today!

968
00:53:48,889 --> 00:53:51,456
Please get home safely.

969
00:53:51,479 --> 00:53:55,358
I will, thanks!

970
00:53:55,381 --> 00:53:57,874
See you the day after tomorrow.

971
00:53:57,898 --> 00:54:00,931
Yes, see you then!

972
00:54:00,954 --> 00:54:02,887
Excuse me.

973
00:54:02,910 --> 00:54:04,410
Scene 29: Ali’s Growth – Becoming a Pro

974
00:54:04,410 --> 00:54:09,544
Ali, you’ve improved so much lately!

975
00:54:09,567 --> 00:54:11,900
Yes, thank you.

976
00:54:11,923 --> 00:54:15,723
You were so nervous at first, remember?

977
00:54:15,746 --> 00:54:19,479
Yes, I was really nervous.

978
00:54:19,502 --> 00:54:22,836
Now you’re like a senior staff member!

979
00:54:22,859 --> 00:54:26,792
Yeah, work has become fun.

980
00:54:26,815 --> 00:54:30,433
You chat with customers a lot now too.

981
00:54:30,456 --> 00:54:34,509
Yes, I’ve even got regulars now.

982
00:54:34,533 --> 00:54:36,984
That’s amazing!

983
00:54:37,007 --> 00:54:40,341
Your Japanese has become so natural too.

984
00:54:40,364 --> 00:54:42,179
Thank you!

985
00:54:42,202 --> 00:54:44,484
It’s all thanks to you, Manager.

986
00:54:44,507 --> 00:54:48,323
No, it’s all your hard work.

987
00:54:48,347 --> 00:54:50,757
I’m really happy.

988
00:54:50,780 --> 00:54:53,647
Let’s keep this up!

989
00:54:53,670 --> 00:54:56,805
Yes, I’ll work even harder.

990
00:54:56,828 --> 00:55:00,028
Is there anything you’re struggling with?

991
00:55:00,051 --> 00:55:03,668
No, nothing for now.

992
00:55:03,692 --> 00:55:06,825
Feel free to talk to me anytime.

993
00:55:06,848 --> 00:55:09,648
I will, thank you.

994
00:55:09,671 --> 00:55:13,004
I’m excited to see how much more you’ll grow.

995
00:55:13,027 --> 00:55:16,394
Me too—I can’t wait!

996
00:55:16,417 --> 00:55:18,150
Thank you.

997
00:55:18,173 --> 00:55:22,269
No, thank *you* for everything.

998
00:55:22,293 --> 00:55:23,793
Scene 30: A Heartfelt Farewell – Gratitude and Goodbyes

999
00:55:23,793 --> 00:55:27,593
Ali, today’s your last day, isn’t it?

1000
00:55:27,616 --> 00:55:30,694
Yes, today is the last day.

1001
00:55:30,718 --> 00:55:33,322
I feel so sad.

1002
00:55:33,345 --> 00:55:37,312
Thank you so much for everything over the past year.

1003
00:55:37,335 --> 00:55:40,747
No, thank *you*.

1004
00:55:40,770 --> 00:55:45,024
Having you here, Ali, was such a big help.

1005
00:55:45,047 --> 00:55:47,014
Thank you!

1006
00:55:47,037 --> 00:55:50,052
I’m really glad I got to work here.

1007
00:55:50,075 --> 00:55:53,842
You’re going to be an amazing professional, Ali.

1008
00:55:53,865 --> 00:55:56,432
Yes, I'll do my best.

1009
00:55:56,455 --> 00:55:59,988
Manager, I’m truly grateful to you.

1010
00:56:00,011 --> 00:56:04,645
Was working in Japan a good experience for you?

1011
00:56:04,669 --> 00:56:07,902
Yes, I’ll never forget it.

1012
00:56:07,925 --> 00:56:10,560
It was such a great experience.

1013
00:56:10,583 --> 00:56:14,550
If you ever need help, you’re always welcome to come by.

1014
00:56:14,573 --> 00:56:16,773
Yes, thank you.

1015
00:56:16,796 --> 00:56:19,283
Can I come visit sometime?

1016
00:56:19,307 --> 00:56:21,640
Of course!

1017
00:56:21,663 --> 00:56:23,930
You’re always welcome here.

1018
00:56:23,953 --> 00:56:27,199
Yes, I’ll definitely come back.

1019
00:56:27,223 --> 00:56:29,090
Goodbye.

1020
00:56:29,114 --> 00:56:30,514
Goodbye.

1021
00:56:30,537 --> 00:56:32,170
Take care.

1022
00:56:32,193 --> 00:56:34,626
You too, Ali. Take care.

1023
00:56:34,649 --> 00:56:36,541
Thank you very much!

1024
00:56:36,565 --> 00:56:38,131
Thank you.